From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: rndis: open the TX filter by default

With the CDC Ethernet functional descriptor in place (patch 0021) the TP26 BIOS
finally brings up its side of the Redfish Host Interface: it runs RNDIS_MSG_INIT
during POST, self-assigns 169.254.0.18 and ARPs for the BMC.  But the link is
receive-only -- usb0 shows RX 800 bytes / 22 packets and TX 0 -- so the ARP is
never answered, no TCP reaches bmcweb, and the inventory push never starts.

f_rndis leaves port.cdc_filter at 0 and relies on the host opening it via
OID_GEN_CURRENT_PACKET_FILTER.  Linux does that; the BIOS never does -- it
INIT/HALT-loops four times and then simply starts sending traffic.  While the
filter is 0, u_ether's eth_start_xmit() drops every outgoing frame:

	/* apply outgoing CDC or RNDIS filters */
	if (skb && !is_promisc(cdc_filter)) { ... }

Every other u_ether-based function (ecm, eem, ncm, subset) initialises the
filter to DEFAULT_FILTER; RNDIS is the exception, and the existing REVISIT
comment in rndis_set_alt() already notes this area has "done this wrong for a
very long time".  Do the same here.

Signed-off-by: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_rndis.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_rndis.c
@@ -603,7 +603,17 @@
 		 * very long time.  We need another call to the link layer
 		 * code -- gether_updown(...bool) maybe -- to do it right.
 		 */
-		rndis->port.cdc_filter = 0;
+		/*
+		 * Open the transmit filter instead of waiting for the host to
+		 * set OID_GEN_CURRENT_PACKET_FILTER.  The TP26 UEFI RNDIS
+		 * driver never sends that OID -- it INIT/HALT-loops and then
+		 * starts sending ARP -- so with a zero filter u_ether's
+		 * eth_start_xmit() silently drops every reply and the link is
+		 * receive-only.  Every other u_ether function (ecm, eem, ncm,
+		 * subset) defaults to DEFAULT_FILTER; RNDIS is the odd one out,
+		 * as the REVISIT comment above concedes.
+		 */
+		rndis->port.cdc_filter = DEFAULT_FILTER;
 
 		DBG(cdev, "RNDIS RX/TX early activation ... \n");
 		net = gether_connect(&rndis->port);
@@ -1041,8 +1051,9 @@
 
 	rndis->port.ioport = netdev_priv(opts->net);
 	mutex_unlock(&opts->lock);
-	/* RNDIS activates when the host changes this filter */
-	rndis->port.cdc_filter = 0;
+	/* RNDIS normally activates when the host changes this filter; open it
+	 * up front so a host that never sets it can still be replied to. */
+	rndis->port.cdc_filter = DEFAULT_FILTER;
 
 	/* RNDIS has special (and complex) framing */
 	rndis->port.header_len = sizeof(struct rndis_packet_msg_type);
